## Context

Found by the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09 (19:05-19:15 UTC, run
from the ~/CNRS session). Four gaps in how worktree locks prove liveness and
how GC and molt treat them.

## Evidence

- (a) A lock reason's pid can name a `claude bg-spare` pool process: pid
  1696669 held the locks of AEDIST t0682 and search-works-for-zotero t0774
  for hours while alive, blocking molt step 0 in both repos. It was dead by
  19:04.
- (b) `worktree-gc.sh` skips a dead-pid locked worktree whose branch still
  exists upstream; a seat removed t0774 by hand after preflight.
- (c) [corrected 2026-11-09: the Claude Code runtime already writes `**/.claude/worktrees/` into info/exclude in the harness, git-erg, arena, search-works-for-zotero and zoteus; absent in DOIfetch; the harness's own registration writes only `/.tmp/`] In repos that do not ignore `.claude/worktrees/` (all but git-erg),
  the primary checkout lists the live worktree as untracked and worktree-gc
  skips it as "uncommitted WIP". The hunt recipe
  (`skills/hunt/SKILL.md` § Worktree) does not add the path to
  `.git/info/exclude`.
- (d) [corrected 2026-11-09: the hook refuses only when the index holds a ticket without its claim or a duplicate number, e.g. a pre-migration base or a staged draft; escape hatches: migrate --claims, add the claim, --no-verify] The pre-commit erg-claims hook refuses any commit on a base older than
  the claims. In an old AEDIST worktree it blocked molt's "commit dirty files
  to a WIP branch" step and left the files staged.

## Diagnosis

Established: the four observations above. Not established for (a): whether
`$PPID` resolves to the pool process because the session was spawned from a
spare, or because the pid was recycled; the lock reason alone cannot tell.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] worktree-gc handles a dead-pid locked worktree whose branch exists upstream (case b): dead pid, clean tree and HEAD equal to its upstream → unlock and remove, branch kept
- [ ] The hunt worktree registration adds `/.claude/worktrees/` to `.git/info/exclude` (next to `/.tmp/`)
- [ ] molt step 1.5 documents the WIP-commit workaround when the claims hook refuses (migrate --claims, restore the claim, or a fresh worktree on origin/main)

## Verify and Imagine (raid 4afdb3, 2026-11-09)
- Verified: (a) live now: this raid's shells have PPID 3046370 = `claude bg-spare --bg-spare
  .../a13e5edc.claim.sock`, up 4 h, child of bg-pty-host 3046358; the raid and hunt worktrees
  raid-1486-1491-3046370-*, t1486-3046370-*, t1491-3046370-* are locked with that pid. A claimed
  spare keeps its bg-spare command line for the session's whole life, so "a bg-spare pid is not a
  live owner" would make gc reclaim live sessions; pid 1696669 that "held locks for hours, dead by
  19:04" fits a real session that ended: (a) may be working as intended. (b) by code order:
  worktree-gc.sh flush() gates on upstream:track != "[gone]" before the lock rail, deliberately.
  (c) partly stale: register_tmp_exclude writes only `/.tmp/`, but the Claude Code runtime writes a
  `# claude-code-runtime` block with `**/.claude/worktrees/` into info/exclude: present in the
  harness, git-erg, arena, search-works-for-zotero (the ticket's claim about swz is contradicted),
  zoteus; absent in DOIfetch; AEDIST unchecked. (d) imprecise: the managed block
  (git-erg src/go/assets/integration.md ~63-85) scans the index for a ticket without its claim or a
  duplicate number; a WIP commit fails only when the index holds unclaimed tickets (pre-migration
  base, or a staged draft without its claim); escape hatches exist (migrate --claims, add the
  claim, --no-verify).
- Path if kept: (b) narrow gc branch after the gone gate: dead pid + clean tree + HEAD == upstream
  → unlock and remove, branch kept (~15 lines, 2 tests in tests/test_worktree_tools.py); (c) second
  line `/.claude/worktrees/` in register_tmp_exclude under the same flock (~5 lines); (d) molt step
  1.5 prose: migrate --claims, restore the claim, or a fresh worktree on origin/main; the hook text
  is git-erg's (ticket there only if the author wants the hook changed). Not a monster; one PR.
  Guards on guards: the lock rail is six cases deep; fix at the source if anything.
- Author decisions: (1) criterion 1: find an observable difference between a claimed and an
  unclaimed spare (children, claim socket state); none → drop criterion 1 and close (a) as working
  as intended; (2) criterion 4: documentation form (recommended) or a git-erg hook change;
  (3) correct Evidence (c) and (d) before anyone implements from them.

## Author decisions (raid 5c2a37, 2026-11-09)
- Criterion 1 dropped (author, 2026-11-09): a claimed bg-spare keeps its command line for the session's life, so rejecting bg-spare pids would reclaim live sessions; (a) closes as working as intended.
- Criterion 4 in documentation form; no git-erg hook change.
- Evidence (c) and (d) corrected below before implementation.
